# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=paladin:holy style=wander size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: paladin:holy has eight prior readings
# (raid/daily/battleground/walk, styles idle/wander/good/melee/flee) but
# never once under mode=clear -- every prior reading was a single standalone
# pull or a single-room walk, never a whole evening. wander+25-heroic has
# been run before on two other specs (priest:discipline, stalled in VIGIL;
# paladin:retribution, crossed clean for six rooms, direction.md #6) but
# never on a healer. wander is also the one style that still presses
# abilities (round-robin through all five slots, scripts/playbot.ts:1020-25)
# while steering nowhere in particular -- unlike idle, which presses nothing.
# README says a heal always targets whoever is furthest from full regardless
# of who cast it or from where, so this is the first chance to see whether a
# healer's own automatic heal-targeting keeps the raid up across multiple
# rooms and pulls even when the body casting it is doing nothing to help
# itself find a fight or stay near one.
#
# A fresh save locks 25-heroic, so #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the tier the
# way every other 25-heroic clear/walk script in this ledger does since the
# 2026-09-26 driver-lesson, then backs out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the
# door rather than the invite's single-fight "visiting" framing.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:paladin:holy
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening wander 80 5
shot end
state
says
bill
